## ============================================================================
## TRANSPORT PLAY-STATE (pull-consistent, 2026-07-28)
## ============================================================================

TRANSPORT_PLAY_STATE:
  invariant: "The play button must NEVER be visible while any audio is playing (founder ruling, Jonathan's staging desync 2026-07-28)."
  isPlaying:
    definition: "computed(() => simplePlayer.isPlaying.value) — a PULL from the engine's current state. Never a writable ref, never synced by a watcher, never manually assigned."
    consumers: "Cycle-scoped logic: speak-gap ring gate (ringProgress), session timer, VAD/adaptation gates, warm-burst-on-pause."
  isAudioPlaying:
    definition: "computed OR of isPlaying + playingPodLapAudio + playingCommentaryAudio + isPlayingWelcome + isPlayingIntroduction + isPreparingToPlay"
    consumers: "The TRANSPORT-facing signal: BottomNav play/stop button (pulled by PlayerContainer via template ref — no event hop), PlayerRestingState overlay gate, wake lock, mediaSession playbackState, is-paused styling, sr-only announcer."
  container_binding: "PlayerContainer.isPlaying = computed(() => learningPlayerRef.value?.isAudioPlaying ?? false). The old @playStateChanged event mirror was REMOVED — edge-triggered mirrors can miss/reorder an emission and show PLAY while the engine is mid-cycle until the next engine toggle re-syncs (the recurring 'reverse polarity' family: fd164f43 attempted this fix 2026-06-09 and was reverted same night in a promote de-risk; the disease then resurfaced on staging 3bfeb1d)."
  tap_dispatch:
    togglePlayback: "Single dispatch for BottomNav tap AND ring tap (handleRingTap delegates). Order: (1) awakening soft-guard — swallow taps while isAwakening UNLESS audio is sounding (re-landed bf281cd1); (2) welcome/introduction/preparing → handlePause; (3) pod/commentary → halt runtime audio; (4) engine playing → handlePause; else handleResume."
    firstPlayPauseRequested: "Pause intent raised by handlePause while a first-play sequence is awaiting its preload/welcome; handleResume's first-play path re-checks it after EVERY await and bails before simplePlayer.play() (re-landed d5243e42 — a stop tap can never be overtaken by audio it can't stop)."
  regression_test: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/transportStateSync.test.ts (late-attach pull reads, same-tick toggle bursts, the mirror-wedging interleave). E2E: e2e/transport-first-cycle-walk.mjs (N fresh-profile cold starts asserting the invariant + gap bar + voice-2 text)."

## ============================================================================
## PULL-CONSISTENT UI STATE (tranche 3, 2026-07-28)
## Full mirror inventory + doctrine: docs/player/pull-consistency-map.md
## ============================================================================

PULL_CONSISTENT_STATE:
  doctrine: "UI state that REPRESENTS engine state is DERIVED (computed reading engine truth), never a writable mirror (ref + edge-triggered watcher + scattered assignments + emit hops). Watchers remain legitimate as bridges to imperative sinks (wake lock, mediaSession, animations) and for genuine accumulators."
  currentPhase:
    definition: "computed: SIMPLE_PHASE_TO_UI[simplePlayer.phase] when rounds are loaded (idle/buffering→prompt, pause→speak, voice1/voice2→voice_1/voice_2); legacyUiPhase ref only on the pre-SimplePlayer path. The old two-hop relay (engine → onPhaseChanged → pendingPhase ref → watcher) plus two legacy writers is deleted."
    consumers: "showTargetText (voice-2 text reveal), phase-strip is-active classes, hero/control-pane classes, ring-progress gate, phaseEnteredAt metric."
    side_effects: "Speak-gap ring start stays an edge (it starts an animation) but keys off simplePlayer.phase directly."
    regression_test: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/phaseDisplaySync.test.ts"
  currentCycle:
    definition: "computed: simplePlayer.currentCycle mapped to the legacy display shape (text fields only — textNative deliberately dropped; romanised primary glyphs come from displayTiling); legacyCycle ref only while the engine has no cycle (pre-SimplePlayer path). The old edge-triggered sync watcher (hold-on-null) + legacy writer are deleted — the displayed text pair is a pure function of the same state that chooses the audio."
    consumers: "currentPhrase (hero text), visibleTexts (QA reporting). Transient engine nulls fall through to '' where the displayedKnownText/TargetText hold-last-good latches (B5) keep the last real text."
    regression_test: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/cycleTextSync.test.ts"
  mode_overlays:
    definition: "isListeningMode / isPronunciationMode = computeds over showListeningOverlay / showPronunciationOverlay, exposed via defineExpose; PlayerContainer pulls them via the template ref. The @listeningModeChanged / @pronunciationModeChanged event mirrors (7 emit sites) are deleted."
  buffering_prompt:
    definition: "bufferingPromptVisible = computed(() => simplePlayer.phase === 'buffering') — was a watcher-synced ref."
  position:
    definition: "currentRoundIndex / currentItemInRound = computeds: simplePlayer.roundIndex/cycleIndex once simplePlayer.isInitialized (new composable signal, set by initialize()), else preEngineRoundIndex/preEngineItemInRound — the single pre-engine resume intent. Writers of the intent: the legacy resume labyrinth (localStorage/DB/fresh-start/generate paths), course-change reset, preview seeding (which routes through jumpToRound instead when the engine already exists), and the legacy useCyclePlayback advancement (authoritative only on that engine-less path). The old writable mirrors (engine watchers + ~20 manual assignments) are deleted; post-init position writes are a compile error — position moves only via engine navigation (jumpToRound/jumpToSeed/jumpToLegoId/stepCycle)."
    consumers: "currentRound (loadedRounds cross-index), sessionProgress, splash/resting position display, rolling-buffer cursors, session-timer/expansion watchers, debug overlay."
    side_effects: "The simplePlayer.roundIndex watcher survives as an effect bridge only (DB cursor persist + instant-playback cursor push + tier-3/lookahead prefetch triggers); the cycleIndex mirror watcher is deleted outright. savePositionToLocalStorage's itemInRound fallback now reads the engine live (the mirror-lag it compensated for is structurally gone)."
    regression_test: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/roundPositionSync.test.ts (pre-engine intent read, intent consumed at init, late-attach pull, post-init wedge-write inertness, same-tick jump burst, boundary walk)."
  belt_position:
    definition: "beltAnchorSeed = computed: INF-PLAY active ? beltFreezeSeed : seed(visualLegoIdForRound(simplePlayer.currentRound)); ONE immediate watcher bridges it into useSharedBeltProgress.setPlayingPosition (cross-surface sink). The INF-PLAY belt freeze is an explicit intent: enterInfPlay / advanceInfPlayRound / infplay-back / enterInfPlayFromCache / both INF-PLAY resume paths write beltFreezeSeed = course-end seed; shape-only INF PLAY with no anchor (stripped rounds, guests) holds the last belt (null anchor writes nothing); exiting INF PLAY clears the freeze. The ~15 scattered setPlayingPosition pushes (incl. deriveBeltFromLandedRound + its 5 callers) are deleted. Pre-engine writers kept by design: the boot-time splash seed and updateBeltForPosition (engine-guarded: legacy boundaries + pre-engine preview only)."
    consumers: "playingBelt / playingBeltProgress / courseProgress in useBeltProgress, belt pill colour + journey bar (beltCssVars keeps its own INF-PLAY red lock)."
    regression_test: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/beltPositionSync.test.ts (main-loop follow through jump interleaves, INF-PLAY freeze no-bounce, guest/shape-only hold, exit unfreeze, late-attach immediate delivery, engine-agreement walk)."

## ============================================================================
## CONSTELLATION NETWORK INTEGRATION
